Carla, thank you - this is a really useful summary, and I'm glad the case packer finding landed, that one surprised us too!

Short version: you'll have a proposal covering all three points by Friday Sept 25, in time for your steering meeting on the 29th. Some context on each so you're not waiting blind:

1. Pricing for Salinas + Yuma, two lines each. We're in the middle of simplifying our packaging for exactly this shape of deal (multi-line, multi-plant, mid-market), and I'd rather quote you the new structure than the old per-line list, because the new one will be better for you. That's the reason for "by the 25th" rather than "by Monday" - I need a couple of weeks to get it signed off internally. If it helps I can send indicative ranges sooner, with the caveat that they're ranges.

2. Base vs add-on. Base covers ingest, the exception view, the daily/weekly reports, SSO and unlimited operator seats. Onboarding services are priced separately and you can decline them (more below). The downtime module: honest answer is it's on the Q4 roadmap and not in the product today, and I'm not going to price something we haven't shipped. What I can do is put in writing that when it ships it's included in your base at no added cost. I'll put that in the proposal.

3. Onboarding timeline. You're right that the workshop ran long, and we've looked at why: your engineer was building the tag mapping from scratch because Salinas had no historian export. For Yuma, which does have one, we'd plan on one day. For Salinas line 2, two days, because half the tags carry over from line 1. So roughly: Yuma three weeks to first report, Salinas line 2 two weeks, and they can run in parallel with Yuki on both. I'll write it up properly with the assumptions stated.

On the comparison with the other two - genuinely happy to be compared, and if it helps I can put you in touch with a customer that runs two lines with us so you can hear the unvarnished version.

One question back: for Yuma, is the plant network owned locally or by corporate IT? It changes who we need in the first week.

Talk soon, and thanks again for the thorough pilot.

Tomás

